[thin] These are the 2.60 mm solid bed-start eye floor at its 0.30 mm bed-facing chamfer. The 2.304 mm local reading approaches that chamfer; the floor is not uniformly 2.304 mm thick. Its upper Z 2.60 is held fixed under the rail's Z 4.04 underside, leaving 1.44 mm lower air while only top air is compared. Every eye begins at the common first model nozzle Z 0.20.
alternatives: Growing the floor upward from the existing bed start to 3.00 mm reduces lower air by 0.40 mm unless the eye/rail geometry is moved. Adding 0.40 mm downward while holding upper Z 2.60 changes the bed origin and common rail-layer schedule. Removing the chamfer enlarges corner stock but removes the intended first-bed release margin.
