click: x=-52.000 y=62.236 z=0.300

[thin] These opposite surfaces bound the 3.00 mm eye side walls: outer Y span 10.30 mm, inner span 4.30 mm. They connect the bedded floor and captive roof around the rail, whose Y running air is 0.35 per face. Both native sides retain 0.335 mm full-width air at the first rail slab Z 4.28 and 0.350 mm from Z 4.52 through 6.20. This describes model stock and commanded lateral air, not physical sliding force.
alternatives: Thickening the side walls outward to 4.00 or 6.00 mm preserves internal air but needs larger basin windows and handle/stop travel clearance. Growing them inward changes the fixed 0.35 per-face running gap. A separately assembled open slider removes the captive side-wall loop and changes the release mechanism.
